# Step 27: prompts at a turn's edges, in `cortex-tui`'s application, which
# both links drive (docs/steps/27/answered.md, point 5). Each rule broken
# one at a time, with the tests that must fail. Written with the code.

# ------------------------------- (1) the held prompts, one at a time

[break] held-prompts-all-go-at-once
rule: The prompts held while the session opened go one at a time: the next is sent only once the one before it was answered.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::send_held
find:
            self.held_sent = Some(self.send_prompt(sent, delivery));
            return;
replace:
            self.held_sent = Some(self.send_prompt(sent, delivery));
caught-by:
    app::tests::prompts::held_prompts_go_one_at_a_time_each_once_the_one_before_is_answered
    app::tests::prompts::a_refused_held_prompt_gives_back_those_behind_it_in_order

[break] the-held-prompts-after-the-first-are-not-queued
rule: Each held prompt after the first is queued behind the one before it.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::send_held
find: (Some(ItemDelivery::Queue), false)
replace: (None, true)
caught-by:
    app::tests::prompts::held_prompts_go_one_at_a_time_each_once_the_one_before_is_answered
    app::tests::prompts::after_a_held_steer_the_next_held_prompt_is_queued

[break] a-refused-held-prompt-lets-the-next-go
rule: A refused held prompt comes back with those behind it, in order, and none of them is sent.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::prompt_answered
find: if refused || sent.stopped
replace: if sent.stopped
caught-by:
    app::tests::prompts::a_refused_held_prompt_gives_back_those_behind_it_in_order
    app::tests::prompts::a_prompt_sent_while_held_ones_are_on_their_way_follows_them

[break] a-prompt-overtakes-the-held-ones-on-their-way
rule: A prompt sent once the session is open, while the held ones are still on their way, follows them.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::submit
find: if self.held_sent.is_some() {
replace: if false {
caught-by:
    app::tests::prompts::a_prompt_sent_while_held_ones_are_on_their_way_follows_them

[break] the-held-prompts-follow-an-interrupt
rule: After an interrupt, the held prompts not sent come back once the one on its way is answered, rather than run after the stop.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::prompt_answered
find: sent.stopped || !self.is_open(&sent.session)
replace: !self.is_open(&sent.session)
caught-by:
    app::tests::prompts::stopping_while_held_prompts_are_on_their_way_gives_back_those_not_sent

[break] new-leaves-the-session-while-held-prompts-are-on-their-way
rule: `/new` does not leave the session while a held prompt is on its way: what follows it is that session's.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state.rs
in: App::new_session
find: if self.running.is_some() || self.held_sent.is_some() {
replace: if self.running.is_some() {
caught-by:
    app::tests::prompts::new_does_not_leave_the_session_while_held_prompts_are_on_their_way

[break] a-switch-leaves-the-session-while-held-prompts-are-on-their-way
rule: A switch in `/sessions` does not leave the session while a held prompt is on its way.
file: crates/cortex-tui/src/app/state/commands.rs
in: App::switch_to
find: if self.running.is_some() || self.held_sent.is_some() {
replace: if self.running.is_some() {
caught-by:
    app::tests::prompts::a_switch_does_not_leave_the_session_while_held_prompts_are_on_their_way

# ------------------------------------ (3) an open onto a running turn

